// Hunger, the body: how fed an agent is, and how that falls (AGENCY.md §6,
// d17).
//
// Cut points:
// - full, reduced, abstract, frozen: alike. `fed` is kept as of `fedAt`, and
//            falls a point every three minutes, computed when read
//            (BGSatiety), so nothing steps it. Going without (fed 10 or less)
//            harms the body a point every ten minutes, fatigue up to 50 and
//            then injury, at every level of detail, frozen included: a frozen
//            agent doesn't decide, so doesn't eat, and starves (open:
//            DETAIL_REGIMES.md).
// - eating:  eating.tri sets `fed` and `fedAt`.
// - feeling: interoception feels hunger as 100 less how fed, less twice the
//            attention the agent's activities take, by bands of 10 (20 when
//            exhausted); its wake is the next band, put off to the cadence's
//            beat below full.
// - code:    src/domains/BGBodies.m: the period, the band, starving and its
//            harm, none of them in content yet; src/know/BGKnowledge.m:
//            interoception.

// What hunger adds to an agent: how fed it is (AGENCY.md §6), 0 to 100, as of
// `fedAt`. It falls a point every three minutes, computed when read.
#Agent: {
    fed:   *80 | int & >=0 & <=100          @field(content, saved, proposable, inspect)
    fedAt: *0ms | time & >=0ms & <=10000d   @field(content, saved, proposable, inspect)
}
